# Terraform working files. None of these may ever be committed; the CI job
# infra-validate fails the build if one is.

# Provider plugins and module cache.
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl.bak

# State. Lives in the S3 backend, never in git: it contains resource ids,
# endpoints, ARNs and anything a provider marks non-sensitive but we would
# rather not publish.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info

# Saved plans. A plan file contains the full resource diff, values included.
*.tfplan
tfplan
plan.out

# Real values. The .example files next to them are the committed templates.
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars
backend.hcl

# Crash logs can contain variable values.
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Override files are a local escape hatch, never a shared one.
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# Only a ROOT module consumes a lock file. `terraform init` leaves one in every
# child module it is run from (CI validates each module separately); those are
# noise. envs/*/.terraform.lock.hcl IS committed, with hashes for every platform
# the team and CI run on.
modules/*/.terraform.lock.hcl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The `secrets` Terraform module is source code, not a secret store.
#
# The repository root .gitignore carries `secrets/` (meant for a local directory
# of credentials), and that pattern matches at any depth — so it silently
# excluded every file under modules/secrets/, including the SSM parameter map
# that is the whole point of the module. Nothing warned: `terraform validate`
# reads the working tree, so it passed while the files were untracked.
#
# Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so the
# directory itself has to be negated first. Deeper .gitignore files win over
# shallower ones, which is why this works from here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Narrow on purpose: `!modules/secrets/**` would also re-include the provider
# binaries under .terraform/, which are hundreds of megabytes.
!modules/secrets/
!modules/secrets/*.tf
